    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "myjSA",
      "x": 1000,
      "y": 140,
      "name": "Temperature adjustment — 320°C",
      "context": "Temperature target adjustment, not live measured temperature. Firmware evidence: source/Core/Threads/UI/logic/TemperatureAdjust.cpp and source/Core/Threads/UI/drawing/color_160x80/draw_temperature_change.cpp. Initial held buttons are ignored until release. F short increments and B short decrements by configured short step; holds use configured long step and accelerate. ReverseButtonTempChangeEnabled swaps direction, so plus/minus display marks reverse with the button setting. Default draw has PLUS LEFT and MINUS RIGHT. OK short or long, or both buttons, saves and exits to previous screen; three seconds idle also saves/exits. No Cancel action. Units C/F; three digits support temperatures through 850F. Typography: Space Grotesk only, using existing size tokens (15px settings labels, 19px settings values, and 30px temperature digits where needed), weight 600. Reuse raster glyph sets; do not introduce utility-only 12px or 24px font sizes. Verified at native 160x80 canvas size; hardware legibility remains to be checked on-device.",
      "reusable": true,
      "clip": true,
      "width": 160,
      "height": 80,
      "fill": "$section-solder-background",
      "layout": "none",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "jF3fY",
          "x": 11,
          "y": 7,
          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$settings-text-color",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 141,
          "content": "Set temperature",
          "fontFamily": "$settings-label-font",
          "fontSize": "$settings-label-size",
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "T90pw",
          "x": 10,
          "y": 42,
          "name": "Increase mark",
          "fill": "$section-solder-color",
          "content": "+",
          "fontFamily": "$settings-value-font",
          "fontSize": "$settings-value-size",
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "cXH5Y",
          "x": 40,
          "y": 34,
          "name": "Temperature",
          "context": "The right edge of this number should be fixed in the same spot, whether the number be two digits, three, or one. ",
          "fill": "$settings-text-color",
          "content": "320",
          "fontFamily": "$settings-value-font",
          "fontSize": "$home-screen-temperature-size",
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "jOsNH",
          "x": 98,
          "y": 43,
          "name": "Unit",
          "fill": "$settings-text-color",
          "content": "°C",
          "fontFamily": "$settings-value-font",
          "fontSize": 17,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "sjP1m",
          "x": 137,
          "y": 42,
          "name": "Decrease mark",
          "fill": "$section-solder-color",
          "content": "-",
          "fontFamily": "$settings-value-font",
          "fontSize": "$settings-value-size",
          "fontWeight": "600"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "lM9hV",
      "x": 1200,
      "y": 140,
      "name": "Confirmation — restore defaults",
      "context": "Firmware behavior (source/Core/Src/settingsGUI.cpp:481-508, 1077-1087): userConfirmation accepts F_SHORT or OK_SHORT to confirm; it cancels on B_SHORT, F_LONG, B_LONG, OK_LONG, or BOTH. There is no timeout. Confirming calls resetSettings(), displays a success warning until dismissal, then reboots. The on-screen mapping emphasizes OK: Reset and Hold OK: Cancel; F_SHORT is an alternate confirm input. The firmware English prompt is “Are you sure you want to restore default settings?” No hold-to-reset safeguard or selected Yes/No state exists. Typography: Space Grotesk only, using existing size tokens (15px settings labels, 19px settings values, and 30px temperature digits where needed), weight 600. Reuse raster glyph sets; do not introduce utility-only 12px or 24px font sizes. Verified at native 160x80 canvas size; hardware legibility remains to be checked on-device.",
      "reusable": true,
      "clip": true,
      "width": 160,
      "height": 80,
      "fill": "$section-advanced-background",
      "layout": "none",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "fTyG8",
          "x": 11,
          "y": 7,
